\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Data structures are 
\f1\b ways of organizing and storing data
\f0\b0  so that operations on that data (like searching, inserting, deleting, sorting) can be done efficiently.\
Think of them as 
\f1\b containers with different shapes and rules
\f0\b0 , each good for certain tasks.\
